# Tom Petty and The Heartbreakers — Mary Jane's Last Dance
# videoId aowSGxim_O8 (TomPettyVEVO, the official music video)
#
# Note: The bar structure here is not guessed from a lyric-aligned tab. It is
# Note: read off Chordify's beat grid for THIS recording, which is machine-timed
# Note: against the same audio: the verse cycle measures G(2 beats) D(2) Am(4),
# Note: and the chorus measures Em7(8) A(8) Em7(8) A(4) G(4). Ultimate Guitar
# Note: prints the same cycle as "Am G Dsus2 Am", which is the same music with
# Note: the barline drawn elsewhere and the sus spelled out.
#
# Note: WHERE THE BARLINE GOES. This was written first as "| Am | G D |" — Am on
# Note: a whole bar, which is how it is conventionally printed — and that was
# Note: wrong. The evidence is the seam: the chord immediately before every
# Note: chorus is Am held TWO beats (Chordify reads "... G:2 D:2 Am:2 Em7:8"),
# Note: and the chorus plainly starts on a downbeat. Two beats of Am can only
# Note: end a bar if that bar is [D D Am Am] — so the phrase is "| Am G | D Am |"
# Note: and the four-beat Am straddles the barline. The analysis got this right
# Note: and the reference had it wrong, which is the failure mode this corpus has
# Note: to be most careful about: a chart graded against a mistaken truth reads
# Note: as an engine defect and costs a day chasing one.
#
# Note: MODE. Aeolian is wrong here: D major carries F#, and it is the chord the
# Note: vamp turns on, so the verse is A Dorian. The chorus A major is the tonic
# Note: borrowed major, not a key change. Published charts all say "Key: Am",
# Note: which is the loose reading of the same thing.
#
# Note: FORM IS WEAK ON THIS SONG. Intro, verse and the instrumental links are
# Note: harmonically identical, so where one ends and the next begins is a
# Note: labelling choice, not a fact. Grade this song on roots, quality and
# Note: vocabulary; read its form score as advisory.
#
# Note: This recording is 48 cents sharp of A440 — the fixture the corpus of
# Note: backing tracks and modern covers structurally could not contain.
